{"name":"Jealous Jellyfish","hex":"#bb0099","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"jealous","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Suspecting rivalry in love; troubled by worries that one might have been replaced in someone's affections; suspicious of a lover's or spouse's fidelity. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","Protective; zealously guarding; careful in the protection of something (or someone) one has or appreciates, especially one's spouse or lover."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To harass or attack (somebody) out of jealousy.","To deliberately make (someone) jealous of another person's (often their partner's) associations with other people."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/jealous"},{"term":"jellyfish","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An almost transparent aquatic animal; any one of the acalephs, especially one of the larger species, having a jellylike appearance.","Any of various species of cnidarians in the subphylum Medusozoa, including box jellyfish (class Cubozoa), true jellyfish (class Scyphozoa), stalked jellyfish (class Staurozoa), and certain hydrozoans.\n The medusa phase of these animals rather than a younger life stage."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/jellyfish"}],"entries":[{"title":"Jealousy","blocks":[{"text":"Jealousy generally refers to the thoughts or feelings of insecurity, fear, and concern over a relative lack of possessions or safety."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fc/%C4%90%C3%A1nh_ghen.JPG/330px-%C4%90%C3%A1nh_ghen.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jealousy"},{"title":"Jellyfish","blocks":[{"text":"Jellyfish, also known as sea jellies or simply jellies, are the medusa-phase of certain gelatinous members of the subphylum Medusozoa, which is a major part of the phylum Cnidaria. Jellyfish are mainly free-swimming marine animals, although a few are anchored to the seabed by stalks rather than being motile. They are made of an umbrella-shaped main body made of mesoglea, known as the bell, and a collection of trailing tentacles on the underside."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/44/Jelly_cc11.jpg/330px-Jelly_cc11.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jellyfish"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/29/L%C3%A1szl%C3%B3_Moholy-Nagy%2C_gelosia%2C_1927%2C_fotomontaggio_%28george_eastman_museum%2C_rochester_NY%29.jpg/500px-L%C3%A1szl%C3%B3_Moholy-Nagy%2C_gelosia%2C_1927%2C_fotomontaggio_%28george_eastman_museum%2C_rochester_NY%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/29/L%C3%A1szl%C3%B3_Moholy-Nagy%2C_gelosia%2C_1927%2C_fotomontaggio_%28george_eastman_museum%2C_rochester_NY%29.jpg/1280px-L%C3%A1szl%C3%B3_Moholy-Nagy%2C_gelosia%2C_1927%2C_fotomontaggio_%28george_eastman_museum%2C_rochester_NY%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/29/L%C3%A1szl%C3%B3_Moholy-Nagy%2C_gelosia%2C_1927%2C_fotomontaggio_%28george_eastman_museum%2C_rochester_NY%29.jpg/500px-L%C3%A1szl%C3%B3_Moholy-Nagy%2C_gelosia%2C_1927%2C_fotomontaggio_%28george_eastman_museum%2C_rochester_NY%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Jealousy (1927), László Moholy-Nagy","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AL%C3%A1szl%C3%B3_Moholy-Nagy%2C_gelosia%2C_1927%2C_fotomontaggio_(george_eastman_museum%2C_rochester_NY).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/58/Iscenesatt_situasjon%2C_1900_%2814650042212%29.jpg/500px-Iscenesatt_situasjon%2C_1900_%2814650042212%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x